WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:01.240
- All right, let's wrap up

00:00:01.240 --> 00:00:02.790
with something trending on the internet

00:00:02.790 --> 00:00:04.748
you may have missed,
this is what I'm liking.

00:00:04.748 --> 00:00:08.680
(rock music)
(audience cheering)

00:00:08.680 --> 00:00:10.397
It's not easy being a mama of young kids

00:00:10.397 --> 00:00:12.450
and moving to a new city,

00:00:12.450 --> 00:00:15.180
so when Haley relocated
from Houston to Fort Worth,

00:00:15.180 --> 00:00:16.650
she decided to form connections

00:00:16.650 --> 00:00:18.450
by launching a little Facebook group

00:00:18.450 --> 00:00:20.640
she called "The Weird Moms Club."

00:00:20.640 --> 00:00:22.890
She thought she'd make
maybe a few friends.

00:00:22.890 --> 00:00:24.030
That was five years ago.

00:00:24.030 --> 00:00:26.130
Now she's got a whole
community around her.

00:00:26.130 --> 00:00:28.440
The group has thousands of members

00:00:28.440 --> 00:00:31.530
and has even become a
not-for-profit, which is incredible.

00:00:31.530 --> 00:00:32.910
Let's say hi to Haley watching

00:00:32.910 --> 00:00:34.620
on NBC 5 Dallas-Fort Worth.

00:00:34.620 --> 00:00:35.595
What's up, Haley?

00:00:35.595 --> 00:00:37.508
(audience cheering)
- Hi, Kelly.

00:00:37.508 --> 00:00:38.775
Hi, hi, hi.

00:00:38.775 --> 00:00:39.852
- [Kelly] What's up, girl?

00:00:39.852 --> 00:00:40.732
- This is so surreal.

00:00:40.732 --> 00:00:42.216
- [Kelly] Oh, it's nice
to have a Texan on.

00:00:42.216 --> 00:00:43.800
- Thank you so much for having me.

00:00:43.800 --> 00:00:44.633
- Yeah, absolutely.

00:00:44.633 --> 00:00:46.500
How'd you get this started?

00:00:46.500 --> 00:00:48.894
- Well, like you mentioned, I relocated

00:00:48.894 --> 00:00:52.140
from Houston to Fort
Worth about five years ago

00:00:52.140 --> 00:00:53.880
and my husband is from Fort Worth.

00:00:53.880 --> 00:00:55.470
This is his hometown.

00:00:55.470 --> 00:00:57.720
And so, he had all the
friends and the family

00:00:57.720 --> 00:01:00.360
and the connections, and
they're great people,

00:01:00.360 --> 00:01:03.330
but they weren't my people.

00:01:03.330 --> 00:01:04.163
- Yeah.

00:01:04.163 --> 00:01:05.790
- I was a working mom, still am.

00:01:05.790 --> 00:01:07.950
My kids were a lot younger at the time,

00:01:07.950 --> 00:01:09.510
they were two and seven.

00:01:09.510 --> 00:01:12.360
And so, it was really
hard for me to get out

00:01:12.360 --> 00:01:14.673
and make those connections for myself.

00:01:15.660 --> 00:01:17.880
So, I ended up joining a book club

00:01:17.880 --> 00:01:20.250
and hit it off with another mom here,

00:01:20.250 --> 00:01:22.320
and we joked like,
"We're not regular moms,

00:01:22.320 --> 00:01:25.770
we're weird moms," you know,
'cause we have piercings

00:01:25.770 --> 00:01:26.730
and we don't like wine.

00:01:26.730 --> 00:01:28.256
We like whiskey.

00:01:28.256 --> 00:01:29.740
- We don't like wine.

00:01:29.740 --> 00:01:32.190
- We don't fit that
stereotypical mom mold.

00:01:32.190 --> 00:01:33.630
And we were joking around

00:01:33.630 --> 00:01:37.140
and I said, "There's gotta
be more moms like us, right?"

00:01:37.140 --> 00:01:39.930
Especially here in Fort Worth.

00:01:39.930 --> 00:01:42.360
Created the Facebook group
and it's been five years

00:01:42.360 --> 00:01:44.670
and now we have over 2000 members.

00:01:44.670 --> 00:01:48.030
- So, explain how it's a nonprofit.

00:01:48.030 --> 00:01:51.150
- Well, the nonprofit, so
in the 2000 plus members

00:01:51.150 --> 00:01:53.460
we have now in "Weird Moms,"

00:01:53.460 --> 00:01:56.700
I was really lucky to be
able to find a group of women

00:01:56.700 --> 00:02:00.630
that I can depend on and
call them my framily.

00:02:00.630 --> 00:02:03.510
And so, we started swapping
clothes amongst ourselves

00:02:03.510 --> 00:02:05.550
for our kids and ourselves.

00:02:05.550 --> 00:02:07.710
We kind of opened it up to weird moms.

00:02:07.710 --> 00:02:10.350
And so, we went from
swapping with like 10 people

00:02:10.350 --> 00:02:12.090
to a thousand people.

00:02:12.090 --> 00:02:15.240
And then we were able to
incorporate, found the nonprofit,

00:02:15.240 --> 00:02:17.216
and really open it up to the community.

00:02:17.216 --> 00:02:21.360
So since April we've
distributed over 4,000 pounds

00:02:21.360 --> 00:02:23.550
of clothes at no charge

00:02:23.550 --> 00:02:25.960
to almost 800 shoppers here in the area.

00:02:25.960 --> 00:02:27.080
(audience clapping)
- That is so cool.

00:02:29.293 --> 00:02:32.340
Girl, I was that kid
who grew up in church.

00:02:32.340 --> 00:02:34.890
Like they'd have like, they'd
collect bags of clothes

00:02:34.890 --> 00:02:35.730
that, you know, hand me downs.

00:02:35.730 --> 00:02:36.563
- Exactly.

00:02:36.563 --> 00:02:37.890
- I grew up on all that, so that's so cool

00:02:37.890 --> 00:02:39.690
because it's embarrassing for kids

00:02:39.690 --> 00:02:41.490
to show up in the same outfit every day

00:02:41.490 --> 00:02:43.320
and not everybody has that money.

00:02:43.320 --> 00:02:44.400
And especially when you have a lot of kids

00:02:44.400 --> 00:02:46.260
in your household, that's a lot of money.

00:02:46.260 --> 00:02:48.015
So, that's so cool what you're doing.

00:02:48.015 --> 00:02:51.420
It's got a really big
impact on those kids' lives

00:02:51.420 --> 00:02:52.830
at school too, socially speaking.

00:02:52.830 --> 00:02:53.663
So thank you.

00:02:53.663 --> 00:02:55.650
That's so cool.
- Definitely.

00:02:55.650 --> 00:02:57.675
- Haley, I'm liking your right now.

00:02:57.675 --> 00:02:59.730
(audience clapping)

00:02:59.730 --> 00:03:00.750
All right, well that's not all.

00:03:00.750 --> 00:03:02.610
Our season long partner Pilot Pen,

00:03:02.610 --> 00:03:05.160
makers of Precise, the go-to pen

00:03:05.160 --> 00:03:06.360
of "The Kelly Clarkson Show"

00:03:06.360 --> 00:03:08.370
want to celebrate those
bringing people together

00:03:08.370 --> 00:03:10.770
just like you, so they're
gonna give you $1,000.

00:03:10.770 --> 00:03:11.643
How's that sound?

00:03:11.643 --> 00:03:14.643
(audience clapping)

00:03:16.316 --> 00:03:17.149
That should help.

00:03:17.149 --> 00:03:20.528
- [Haley] I am speechless, thank you.

00:03:20.528 --> 00:03:24.623
- Thank you so much from
one weird mom to another.

00:03:24.623 --> 00:03:26.760
Thank you to all our
guests, Michael Buble,

00:03:26.760 --> 00:03:28.290
Alexa and Harry Byrd.

00:03:28.290 --> 00:03:31.530
Y'all have a great day, and if
it's not, try and change it.

